  "correction_id": "B-COR-0012",
  "rule_id": "B-R-009",
  "note": "Partly. We do match one enterprise wire to several invoices, but only using the remittance advice, not just because the open invoice total happens to agree. If there's no remittance advice or it doesn't tie to the invoices, don't auto-match it; send it to ar_lead.",
  "explanation": "The controller confirmed part of B-R-009. They do match one customer wire to several invoices, but only from a remittance advice that ties to those invoices, not because the open invoice total happens to agree. If there's no remittance advice or it doesn't tie, the wire goes to ar_lead. The rule language can't check a remittance advice, so B-R-009 becomes executable false and an investigator handles these wires. The `when` conditions stay the same, so the rule still covers only customer wires whose open invoices in 1200 agree exactly. This keeps the rule from taking over short wires that B-R-022 and B-R-010 already handle. I also approved the rule, since the controller confirmed this corrected version."
 }
